Governance and Accountability
Scope & Core Inquiries: Does this organization demonstrate genuine integrity, fiduciary duty, and accountability across its leadership, supply chains, and host communities? Does leadership suppress adverse scientific findings, retaliate against whistleblowers, conceal conflicts of interest, or maintain extreme CEO-to-worker pay disparities alongside mass layoffs? Does the company engage in bribery, extortion, money laundering, sanctions evasion, aggressive offshore tax haven schemes, or lucrative ties with corrupt and authoritarian regimes? In its international supply chains and resource extraction, does it profit from child labor, forced labor, hazardous sweatshop conditions, or conflict minerals, and does it enforce rigorous, unannounced human rights audits? Within the communities where it physically operates, does it extract massive taxpayer subsidies while disinvesting locally, destabilize regional economies, infringe on indigenous rights, or disproportionately site hazardous and polluting facilities in marginalized, low-income neighborhoods (environmental racism)?